    <statement><p>Consider the function <m>f(x) = x^{2}e^{12 x}</m>.</p>
<p>For this function there are three important intervals:
 <m>(-\infty, A]</m>, <m>[A,B]</m>, and <m>[B,\infty)</m> where
 <m>A</m> and  <m>B</m> are the critical numbers.</p>
<p>Find <m>A</m> <fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
<p>and  <m>B</m> <fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0002"/></p>
<p>For each of the following intervals, tell whether <m>f(x)</m>
is increasing (type in INC) or decreasing (type in DEC).</p>
<p><m>(-\infty, A]</m>: <fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0003"/></p>
<p><m>[A,B]</m>: <fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0004"/></p>
<p><m>[B,\infty)</m> <fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0005"/></p>
</statement>
